# Melos

## Workspace

- Melos 7.x has **no standalone `melos.yaml` file**. All config (scripts, ide,
  command hooks) lives under a `melos:` key in the root `pubspec.yaml`.
- Package discovery uses the native Dart pub `workspace:` list in the root
  `pubspec.yaml` — this is the single source of truth for member packages.
- Each member package's `pubspec.yaml` must have `resolution: workspace`.
- **Always** `melos bootstrap` after any `pubspec.yaml` change.
- **Never** `flutter pub get` directly in workspace packages.
- Scripts with args must be run as `melos run <script> -- <args>` — passing
  `--flags` directly to `melos <script>` is intercepted by Melos itself and
  will fail (e.g. use `melos run feature:create -- orders shared`, not
  `melos feature:create orders --shared`).

## Package Naming

`snake_case`, describes domain: `auth`, `network`, `design_system`
All packages: `publish_to: none`

## New Package

**Infrastructure / shared packages** (stay under `packages/`):
1. Create `packages/<name>/` with `pubspec.yaml` (include `resolution: workspace`)
2. Add to root `pubspec.yaml` `workspace:` list
3. Run `melos bootstrap`

**Feature packages** (go under `packages/features/`):
1. Use `melos run feature:create -- <name> shared` — scaffolds into `packages/features/<name>/`
2. Or create manually under `packages/features/<name>/` and register as `packages/features/<name>` in workspace
3. Run `melos bootstrap`

## Scripts

| Script | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `melos bootstrap` | Link local packages, run pub get |
| `melos analyze` | Full workspace analyze (CI only) |
| `melos test` | Run tests across packages |
| `melos format` | Check formatting |
| `melos check` | format + analyze + test (pre-commit) |
| `melos ci` | bootstrap + check (CI entry) |
| `melos build:provider:android` | Release APK |
| `melos build:client:android` | Release APK |

## melos exec

Run command in each package: `melos exec --scope=<name> -- <command>`

## When NOT to Run

- Do **not** run `melos analyze` during development — per-package `flutter analyze` instead
- Do **not** run `melos check` during routine development — pre-commit only
